WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.309
Hi, I'm Sparrow!

00:00:02.309 --> 00:00:06.044
jev-linkmap rebuilt a whole site's internal links in under six seconds.

00:00:06.044 --> 00:00:08.760
Here's how it decides where each link goes.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:14.017
The trick: a plain script proposes phrases already on the page, so

00:00:14.017 --> 00:00:16.229
the model only answers yes or no.

00:00:16.229 --> 00:00:18.757
And the link lands inside a real sentence.

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:25.575
First, score page pairs by TF-IDF, with each page's headings counted four times.

00:00:25.995 --> 00:00:28.467
Drop pages half the site already links to.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:29.393
That's menu chrome.

00:00:29.813 --> 00:00:33.520
Keep only two-to-six-word phrases already in the page's own copy.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.147
And mask anything already linked, so nothing is linked twice.

00:00:38.842 --> 00:00:42.844
Each candidate becomes a question for Jev: does this link belong, and

00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:44.512
which phrase should carry it?

00:00:44.512 --> 00:00:47.180
Eight thousand four hundred and sixty link decisions.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.506
A rubric sets the instructions and two thresholds.

00:00:50.506 --> 00:00:54.501
Past that gate, two thousand three hundred and eighty-three yeses remain.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:58.202
Then a hard cap of three links per page, not the model,

00:00:58.202 --> 00:01:00.116
cuts that to six hundred and seventy-nine.

00:01:00.536 --> 00:01:04.046
An editor sees one sentence per link, cuts when in doubt, and

00:01:04.046 --> 00:01:05.508
keeps two hundred and eighty-seven.

00:01:06.967 --> 00:01:11.192
A System 2 loop rewrote the rubric twice, lifting recall from

00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:12.729
forty-five to sixty-five percent.

00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:16.186
Moving just the two thresholds gets sixty-four point two.

00:01:17.725 --> 00:01:21.311
The model answers yes or no; the candidates, the cap and the

00:01:21.311 --> 00:01:23.104
thresholds shape most of what ships.

00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:29.843
To recap: candidates from the author's words, yes or no questions, and

00:01:29.843 --> 00:01:31.856
thresholds doing most of the work.

00:01:32.277 --> 00:01:34.395
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:34.395 --> 00:01:35.000
I'm Sparrow.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:35.303
Bye!
